  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nHigh pressure cresting overhead will provide optimal radiational\ncooling conditions tonight with lows dropping into the 20s and\nteens. Temperatures rebounds into the 50s to low 60s Saturday\nunder sunny skies. Saturday night will not be as cold as tonight\nwhile most spots drop into the 20s. Temperatures warm Sunday\ninto Monday as the high shifts offshore. A dry cold front\ncrosses late Monday with another cool Canadian high pressure\nsettling over the area for much of next week. Ensembles show\nlittle in the way of precipitation chances through the end of\nthe month with the next signal for precipitation arriving around\nNovember 1st.",
